    "q-107860": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107860",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Evaluate $\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\,Γ(\\frac{9}{2}).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\,Γ(\\frac{9}{2}) & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot Γ(\\frac{7}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{\\pi }}{15}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\  & =7\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
