    "q-107855": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107855",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Evaluate $4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2}).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) & =\\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{\\pi }}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\,Γ(\\frac{5}{2})=4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }=3\\pi .\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
